WEBVTT

00:00:08.660 --> 00:00:10.160
Shimamura.

00:00:18.450 --> 00:00:20.410
"-1 day before-"

00:00:20.700 --> 00:00:25.160
I somehow ended up back here again.

00:00:25.160 --> 00:00:28.790
Why did we have to become second-years?

00:00:28.790 --> 00:00:34.750
Down below, Shimamura and our
new classmates are having PE class.

00:00:36.540 --> 00:00:41.660
Does Shimamura even realize I'm up here?

00:00:41.660 --> 00:00:45.410
Before I realized it, Shimamura
was surrounded by new people,

00:00:45.410 --> 00:00:49.410
and things were going well for her,
but not for me.

00:00:49.410 --> 00:00:53.500
To put it simply, that's all there is to it.

00:00:53.500 --> 00:00:59.410
Shimamura was smiling...
with people she barely knew.

00:00:59.410 --> 00:01:03.950
And I couldn't find a difference in
that smile with the one she showed me.

00:01:03.950 --> 00:01:08.160
It frustrated me, I couldn't breathe,
and I felt like crying.

00:01:08.160 --> 00:01:12.870
Could it be that there was never
anything actually dramatic or special

00:01:12.870 --> 00:01:16.660
between Shimamura and I?

00:01:29.200 --> 00:01:30.950
Shimamura...

00:03:21.370 --> 00:03:24.120
Is she a third-year?

00:03:24.120 --> 00:03:31.160
As she sat a little further down,
she started to read her book quietly.

00:03:31.160 --> 00:03:35.120
This calm takes over the area

00:03:35.120 --> 00:03:38.410
and I lose my place even here.

00:03:41.540 --> 00:03:44.580
Oh, hey.

00:03:44.580 --> 00:03:48.660
Sorry for taking your spot.

00:03:50.120 --> 00:03:51.290
It's fine.

00:03:52.750 --> 00:03:57.830
I actually knew that Shimamura
would never show up there.

00:03:57.830 --> 00:04:00.040
Shimamura and I aren't alike.

00:04:00.040 --> 00:04:04.830
The reason we even met in
the gym was because I'm alone

00:04:04.830 --> 00:04:08.500
and Shimamura was bored and left class.

00:04:08.500 --> 00:04:10.910
That's all there is to it.

00:04:15.120 --> 00:04:18.700
Before I realized it, I ended up here.

00:04:18.700 --> 00:04:23.000
What I ended up remembering
were precious times with Shimamura.

00:04:26.120 --> 00:04:28.790
It's so boring. Everything's so boring.

00:04:28.790 --> 00:04:32.250
It's so boring without Shimamura around.

00:04:44.370 --> 00:04:48.160
Maybe Shimamura would like something like that.

00:04:49.410 --> 00:04:51.700
I'm an idiot.

00:04:51.700 --> 00:04:56.540
Why am I looking for something
Shimamura might like even now?

00:05:00.370 --> 00:05:01.580
S-Sorry.

00:05:01.580 --> 00:05:03.370
Sorry.

00:05:11.000 --> 00:05:14.330
Oh, hey. I think you dropped this.

00:05:16.080 --> 00:05:19.450
That's... Yeah, I did!

00:05:22.580 --> 00:05:26.750
Thank you. Thank you so much!

00:05:26.750 --> 00:05:29.040
I wonder if it was that important.

00:05:29.040 --> 00:05:30.750
You know...

00:05:30.750 --> 00:05:32.910
I'd never been interested in stuff like that,

00:05:32.910 --> 00:05:35.250
but if I had a matching one with Shimamura...

00:05:37.080 --> 00:05:39.290
I'm doing it again.

00:06:02.080 --> 00:06:06.160
Why... Why am I crying?

00:06:07.660 --> 00:06:10.620
This was basically a mirror.

00:06:10.620 --> 00:06:13.040
I can't stay here.

00:06:13.040 --> 00:06:16.910
Right now, I'm the same
as that puppy on display.

00:06:16.910 --> 00:06:21.000
Actually, I pretty much put myself in that case

00:06:21.000 --> 00:06:25.870
and instead of being able to attract customers,
I'm just sitting there.

00:06:25.870 --> 00:06:28.250
Welcome.

00:06:28.290 --> 00:06:31.040
"Money, marriage, relationships,
I'll predict it all!!"

00:06:32.500 --> 00:06:34.750
Have a seat.

00:06:35.750 --> 00:06:37.910
Are you sure?

00:06:37.910 --> 00:06:41.370
If you go home with troubles in your heart,

00:06:41.370 --> 00:06:44.910
you'll never be able to welcome
a wonderful tomorrow.

00:06:45.910 --> 00:06:48.700
Come, now.

00:06:48.700 --> 00:06:52.040
Um... Are you a fortuneteller?

00:06:52.040 --> 00:06:56.080
Yes, or perhaps, a fortunegiver.

00:06:56.080 --> 00:06:57.700
Right...

00:06:57.700 --> 00:07:00.750
I'll tell you anything you need to know. Even...

00:07:00.750 --> 00:07:03.830
...the reason behind those tears.

00:07:04.870 --> 00:07:06.200
Simply put...

00:07:06.200 --> 00:07:08.370
You must be having romance troubles!

00:07:08.370 --> 00:07:09.830
Huh? What?!

00:07:09.830 --> 00:07:11.000
That'll be 1,000 yen.

00:07:11.000 --> 00:07:12.040
Huh?

00:07:15.040 --> 00:07:18.200
Okay, here's--

00:07:18.200 --> 00:07:19.700
Thanks kindly.

00:07:20.700 --> 00:07:24.250
Now, then. Let me just ask you one thing.

00:07:24.250 --> 00:07:28.410
Does that person have longer hair than you?

00:07:28.410 --> 00:07:30.540
That person?

00:07:30.540 --> 00:07:32.410
The one that's very dear to you.

00:07:34.160 --> 00:07:40.250
Shimamura's hair... is so smooth
and pretty... and soft...

00:07:41.500 --> 00:07:43.330
I see.

00:07:43.330 --> 00:07:49.040
If you're already lost in thought,
I think I got the idea.

00:07:49.040 --> 00:07:53.790
Basically, what you are lacking...
is enthusiasm!

00:07:53.790 --> 00:07:58.000
You were worried about how
others view you and ran away.

00:07:58.000 --> 00:08:00.120
It's very obvious what you're lacking.

00:08:00.120 --> 00:08:05.830
I'll tell you a very simple way
you can gain enthusiasm.

00:08:05.830 --> 00:08:10.160
Face that direction and scream.
Right here, right now.

00:08:11.200 --> 00:08:12.540
What?!

00:08:12.540 --> 00:08:16.450
If you don't, you'll just waste your 1,000 yen.

00:08:16.450 --> 00:08:19.660
But if this is what you truly wish for...

00:08:19.660 --> 00:08:22.910
I mean, do I really have to do it
right here and now?

00:08:22.910 --> 00:08:26.790
Do it, if you don't want to have any regrets.

00:08:26.790 --> 00:08:32.040
Now, scream! Scream everything
you're feeling with all your might!

00:08:34.250 --> 00:08:37.500
Throw your arms up and declare it!

00:08:37.500 --> 00:08:41.790
That's the only way you're going to be able
to embrace and steel your heart.

00:08:43.540 --> 00:08:46.120
I-I'll do it...

00:08:46.120 --> 00:08:49.120
Your voice is too soft and
that wasn't the best line.

00:08:49.120 --> 00:08:51.500
And you didn't throw up your arms.

00:08:53.080 --> 00:08:57.910
You're thinking, "If I had the guts to do that,
I wouldn't have this issue."

00:08:57.910 --> 00:09:04.330
Actually, this whole issue
would be resolved if you had guts.

00:09:04.330 --> 00:09:07.040
Now, one more time.

00:09:07.040 --> 00:09:10.200
I-I'm gonna do my best...

00:09:10.200 --> 00:09:12.870
But you're clearly not. Now, one more time.

00:09:12.870 --> 00:09:15.040
Huh? Uh...

00:09:15.040 --> 00:09:16.910
You don't want to have any regrets, do you?

00:09:16.910 --> 00:09:20.040
Then you mustn't run away.

00:09:20.040 --> 00:09:21.910
Run away...

00:09:21.910 --> 00:09:24.450
There's something I can't seem to get over.

00:09:24.450 --> 00:09:28.830
I ended up just denying how I felt
and just ran away from the start.

00:09:28.830 --> 00:09:33.790
But if I'd just stopped and
actually talked to Shimamura,

00:09:33.790 --> 00:09:37.830
none of this would've happened.
A part of me regretted that.

00:09:39.450 --> 00:09:41.370
I won't run away.

00:09:43.790 --> 00:09:46.790
I'm not going to run away!

00:09:46.790 --> 00:09:50.540
Ooh, excellent. Now, one more time.

00:09:53.660 --> 00:09:59.330
I'm not going to run away!

00:09:59.330 --> 00:10:03.080
Wow, you actually did it.

00:10:03.080 --> 00:10:06.750
People don't need to know the future.

00:10:06.750 --> 00:10:09.830
They need to strongly desire the future.

00:10:13.450 --> 00:10:15.160
Um, thanks, I--

00:10:15.160 --> 00:10:19.120
Now, if you'll excuse me.
May you have a bright future!

00:10:19.120 --> 00:10:20.830
You again?

00:10:21.830 --> 00:10:24.620
Retreat!

00:10:27.540 --> 00:10:31.120
Once the weekend is over, I'll tell Shimamura...

00:10:31.120 --> 00:10:35.290
Or so I told myself and actually came
to school, but still, I ended up here.

00:10:35.290 --> 00:10:36.120
"<i>Thunderheads and Rain</i>
Eiji Kikkawa"

00:10:36.120 --> 00:10:38.040
"<i>Thunderheads and Rain</i>
Eiji Kikkawa"

00:10:36.120 --> 00:10:38.040
This book...

00:10:38.620 --> 00:10:42.250
Sorry for taking your spot.

00:10:43.540 --> 00:10:45.250
"<i>Thunderheads and Rain</i>
Eiji Kikkawa"

00:10:47.700 --> 00:10:53.250
"Why did I keep running? Because I was scared.

00:10:53.250 --> 00:10:55.160
I spend every day afraid thinking about

00:10:55.160 --> 00:10:59.000
what if my tomorrow becomes
yesterday to the rest of the world

00:10:59.000 --> 00:11:01.200
as I waste time hesitating.

00:11:01.200 --> 00:11:05.750
If I'm going to be left behind because of
some great change I don't know about,

00:11:05.750 --> 00:11:10.660
I'd rather run to the front and choose a path
where I can make the change myself."

00:11:14.120 --> 00:11:15.750
Left behind...

00:11:16.750 --> 00:11:19.040
I'm not a second-year.

00:11:19.040 --> 00:11:22.500
Only Shimamura was able
to become a second-year.

00:11:22.500 --> 00:11:24.870
Shimamura is in class right now.

00:11:24.870 --> 00:11:29.250
She's eating lunch. She's not coming here.

00:11:29.250 --> 00:11:33.250
There's no reason she would.
Okay, I've got to do this.

00:11:38.290 --> 00:11:42.080
I'm not going to run away!

00:11:42.080 --> 00:11:43.830
Yeah, Yamada.

00:11:43.830 --> 00:11:45.540
Being in a club is sort of a pain.

00:11:45.540 --> 00:11:48.290
--There's no room
in the place I want to go.
--They're so annoying.

00:11:48.290 --> 00:11:50.000
--But...
--Relationships are so hard.
--You can say that again.

00:11:50.000 --> 00:11:51.790
--Relationships are so hard.
--You can say that again.

00:11:51.790 --> 00:11:55.040
--Then I'll just have to make room.
--By the way, on our way home,
wanna get pancakes again?

00:11:55.040 --> 00:11:56.410
Totally!

00:11:56.410 --> 00:11:58.330
What about you, Shi--?

00:11:58.330 --> 00:11:59.830
Shimamura.

00:12:14.370 --> 00:12:18.910
And that was my official start
as a second-year in high school.

00:12:20.500 --> 00:12:24.080
I wonder how long it'd been
since I heard Adachi's voice.

00:12:24.080 --> 00:12:29.200
I think this was the first time
in this classroom.

00:12:29.200 --> 00:12:31.660
Can I sit next to you?

00:12:31.660 --> 00:12:35.330
Huh? Uh, let me get you a seat...

00:12:38.120 --> 00:12:40.160
Right here is fine.

00:12:40.160 --> 00:12:42.370
I see...

00:12:42.370 --> 00:12:45.330
Oh, Shimamura. I bought some breads.

00:12:46.410 --> 00:12:50.290
Huh? This many? Isn't this a bit much?

00:12:50.290 --> 00:12:53.910
You can have whichever one you want, Shimamura.

00:12:53.910 --> 00:12:56.660
Huh? I, um...

00:13:03.410 --> 00:13:05.450
Okay, I'll take one.

00:13:05.450 --> 00:13:08.750
I think I'll have the jam bread.

00:13:08.750 --> 00:13:10.040
Do you want another one?

00:13:10.040 --> 00:13:13.830
N-No, I can't eat that many.

00:13:15.290 --> 00:13:16.700
It was a little embarrassing,

00:13:16.700 --> 00:13:22.120
but I think she made up her mind
that I'm the only one she needed.

00:13:22.120 --> 00:13:24.410
I wonder about me, though...

00:13:24.410 --> 00:13:29.950
There are times if I even really need anyone,
and I still don't have an answer.

00:13:29.950 --> 00:13:33.370
What I did know was my flimsy relationship
with Sancho and the others

00:13:33.370 --> 00:13:38.540
would fade away even before
we changed seats again.

00:13:41.830 --> 00:13:43.910
Shimamura.

00:13:43.910 --> 00:13:47.200
Um, let's go home together.

00:13:53.580 --> 00:13:55.080
Sure.

00:13:56.250 --> 00:13:58.120
Were you just teasing me?

00:13:58.120 --> 00:13:59.910
Not at all.

00:14:05.870 --> 00:14:07.750
That strap...

00:14:11.620 --> 00:14:13.580
Are these popular right now?

00:14:13.580 --> 00:14:16.580
I think they are.

00:14:16.580 --> 00:14:18.080
Where did you buy it?

00:14:18.080 --> 00:14:19.700
Did you want one?

00:14:19.700 --> 00:14:22.750
Yeah, I was thinking of getting one, too...

00:14:22.750 --> 00:14:25.750
Then we'd be matching...

00:14:25.750 --> 00:14:27.870
Huh...?

00:14:27.870 --> 00:14:32.870
So if Adachi got one, she'd be
matching with me and Tarumi.

00:14:32.870 --> 00:14:34.910
I don't really think so...

00:14:34.910 --> 00:14:36.910
Huh?

00:14:36.910 --> 00:14:39.660
U-Um, can I hold your hand?

00:14:39.660 --> 00:14:41.950
Huh? Oh...

00:14:41.950 --> 00:14:44.330
Here you go.

00:14:45.790 --> 00:14:49.870
Why does everyone want to
hold my hand so badly?

00:14:49.870 --> 00:14:54.370
Do they all think I'm going
to wander off somewhere?

00:14:54.370 --> 00:14:57.620
Come to think of it,
Tarumi takes my left hand,

00:14:57.620 --> 00:14:59.830
but Adachi takes my right.

00:15:01.080 --> 00:15:03.830
Okay, Adachi. I'll see you later.

00:15:03.830 --> 00:15:06.620
You've got your bike, right?

00:15:06.620 --> 00:15:08.330
Yeah...

00:15:08.330 --> 00:15:10.120
We'll see each other tomorrow.

00:15:10.120 --> 00:15:11.080
Yeah.

00:15:11.080 --> 00:15:12.830
You're coming to school, right?

00:15:12.830 --> 00:15:14.410
Yeah...

00:15:14.410 --> 00:15:17.370
Because I want to see you...

00:15:17.370 --> 00:15:18.370
Huh?

00:15:18.370 --> 00:15:20.830
No, it's nothing.

00:15:20.830 --> 00:15:23.040
Say, Adachi.

00:15:23.040 --> 00:15:26.160
I can't actually go home
unless you let go of my hand.

00:15:28.620 --> 00:15:31.160
Y-You're not going anywhere...

00:15:31.160 --> 00:15:32.370
Huh?

00:15:32.370 --> 00:15:38.620
You're not going anywhere. Nope, nope, nope...

00:15:38.620 --> 00:15:42.540
Yeah... She reminds me of a sad little puppy.

00:15:47.660 --> 00:15:49.000
C-Come here a sec.

00:15:49.000 --> 00:15:50.330
Huh?

00:15:50.330 --> 00:15:52.790
U-Uh, Adachi?

00:15:57.200 --> 00:15:59.580
Wh-What's wrong?

00:16:04.540 --> 00:16:06.080
I...

00:16:08.120 --> 00:16:12.000
I-I think you're the best, Shimamura...

00:16:15.410 --> 00:16:20.870
Uh, where did this... uh, hug come from?

00:16:20.870 --> 00:16:23.450
We hadn't done anything in a while, so...

00:16:23.450 --> 00:16:25.580
Done anything?

00:16:25.580 --> 00:16:29.080
Because you were with those other girls...

00:16:31.620 --> 00:16:34.950
Oh, you were jealous?

00:16:36.250 --> 00:16:38.370
What am I going to do with you?

00:16:41.620 --> 00:16:44.790
Does Adachi not only want me
to be her big sister,

00:16:44.790 --> 00:16:48.120
but also her mother?

00:16:48.120 --> 00:16:53.750
If Sancho and the others saw us right now,
they'd really get the wrong idea.

00:17:01.870 --> 00:17:07.040
Well, I've gotta get home, little Sakura.

00:17:07.040 --> 00:17:10.620
Why are you treating me like a little kid?

00:17:10.620 --> 00:17:15.330
Um, can I call you later?

00:17:15.330 --> 00:17:18.000
Call me? Sure?

00:17:18.000 --> 00:17:23.330
I'll call you... around seven.

00:17:23.330 --> 00:17:27.450
But I eat dinner around seven...

00:17:27.450 --> 00:17:29.700
Uh, hello?

00:17:31.200 --> 00:17:34.540
Ah, if it isn't Shimamura!

00:17:34.540 --> 00:17:36.290
Shimamura!

00:17:36.290 --> 00:17:38.160
Sis!

00:17:41.370 --> 00:17:43.700
Would you like some strawberry shortcake?

00:17:43.700 --> 00:17:45.830
Er, I'm good.

00:17:45.830 --> 00:17:48.160
But where did you guys get money for that?

00:17:48.160 --> 00:17:53.410
Um, I think Yachi pulled this cake
out of her pocket.

00:17:53.410 --> 00:17:54.540
Huh?

00:17:54.540 --> 00:17:56.500
Praise me.

00:17:57.790 --> 00:18:01.080
I have decided to become Yashiemon.

00:18:01.080 --> 00:18:03.580
Yashiemon?

00:18:03.580 --> 00:18:06.540
If there's anything you'd like,
Shimamura, just--

00:18:06.540 --> 00:18:09.080
Yeah, sure, let's go home.

00:18:09.080 --> 00:18:12.410
I'm home. Hey...

00:18:12.410 --> 00:18:15.830
Can we have dinner earlier? I'm starving.

00:18:15.830 --> 00:18:18.660
I'm making dinner right now.

00:18:19.750 --> 00:18:22.290
Oh, would you like some sweet crackers?

00:18:22.290 --> 00:18:24.790
Wait, where did you get those?

00:18:25.870 --> 00:18:27.500
Well, I am Yashiemon.

00:18:27.500 --> 00:18:30.160
Do you want to eat earlier
than everyone else then?

00:18:30.160 --> 00:18:33.620
Sure. What's for dinner?

00:18:33.620 --> 00:18:35.660
Yakitori I just bought.

00:18:35.660 --> 00:18:37.000
Huh?

00:18:37.000 --> 00:18:39.830
Why are you chopping it up like that?

00:18:39.830 --> 00:18:42.160
Oh, how exciting.

00:18:44.000 --> 00:18:46.000
I made it...

00:18:46.000 --> 00:18:50.000
Knowing Adachi, she'll probably
call me right at seven.

00:18:50.000 --> 00:18:54.950
I wonder if she's sitting very rigidly
in front of her phone right now.

00:19:00.000 --> 00:19:02.000
"4/21 (Tue)"

00:19:02.000 --> 00:19:03.500
"Adachi
Incoming Call"

00:19:03.870 --> 00:19:06.540
And here we go. Hello?

00:19:06.540 --> 00:19:07.660
Shimamura?

00:19:07.660 --> 00:19:09.790
Yup, that's me.

00:19:09.790 --> 00:19:12.500
Good evening. Are your legs asleep?

00:19:12.500 --> 00:19:14.450
Huh? What?

00:19:14.450 --> 00:19:17.410
H-How did you know?

00:19:17.410 --> 00:19:20.830
It was just a guess. So, what's up?

00:19:20.830 --> 00:19:22.700
What's up?

00:19:22.700 --> 00:19:25.000
I figured you wanted to talk about something.

00:19:25.000 --> 00:19:27.660
No, not really...

00:19:27.660 --> 00:19:31.450
I just hadn't called you for a while...

00:19:31.450 --> 00:19:33.410
Huh...?

00:19:33.410 --> 00:19:35.790
You don't want to make any friends, Adachi?

00:19:35.790 --> 00:19:38.540
Huh? No.

00:19:38.540 --> 00:19:41.200
I'm not really interested.

00:19:42.540 --> 00:19:43.700
And...

00:19:43.700 --> 00:19:45.000
"And"?

00:19:45.000 --> 00:19:48.120
And I have you, Shimamura...

00:19:49.540 --> 00:19:52.200
Did Adachi always talk like this?

00:19:52.200 --> 00:19:56.450
Do you talk to anyone else
on the phone, Shimamura?

00:19:56.450 --> 00:19:59.040
Well, yeah. Sometimes.

00:19:59.040 --> 00:20:00.910
Oh, you do...

00:20:00.910 --> 00:20:02.830
Why do you sound so sad?

00:20:02.830 --> 00:20:06.790
Because I thought I was the only one...

00:20:06.790 --> 00:20:11.500
You're the only one that I call, so...

00:20:11.500 --> 00:20:13.500
...never mind.

00:20:21.790 --> 00:20:24.200
Do you want to just end the call?

00:20:24.200 --> 00:20:25.290
Huh?

00:20:25.290 --> 00:20:28.750
Well, if we're not going to talk,
it's sort of a waste of money.

00:20:28.750 --> 00:20:31.750
N-Not at all! I mean...

00:20:31.750 --> 00:20:34.620
Because then...

00:20:34.620 --> 00:20:36.120
Because then...?

00:20:36.120 --> 00:20:42.250
While I'm on the phone with you,
I get to have your time all to myself...

00:20:43.700 --> 00:20:45.870
Say, Adachi.

00:20:45.870 --> 00:20:48.660
You're a bit possessive.

00:20:48.660 --> 00:20:52.250
Huh? I-I think it's normal.

00:20:52.250 --> 00:20:55.450
Yeah... I don't know about that.

00:20:55.450 --> 00:20:57.620
This is totally normal.

00:20:57.620 --> 00:21:00.870
I think it's normal...

00:21:00.870 --> 00:21:02.370
Well I mean,

00:21:02.370 --> 00:21:07.200
in the end, it's not a bad feeling
knowing that someone cares about you.

00:21:23.120 --> 00:21:25.790
Um, Adachi...?

00:21:30.200 --> 00:21:31.450
"Shimamura
In Call"

00:21:31.450 --> 00:21:33.580
"Shimamura
In Call"

00:21:31.450 --> 00:21:33.580
Are you okay?

00:21:35.790 --> 00:21:38.870
Well... Well...

00:21:38.870 --> 00:21:42.700
Himamuwa... You...

00:21:44.660 --> 00:21:50.120
When I'm with Adachi,
my possibilities are fixed.

00:21:50.120 --> 00:21:55.080
If I had to choose someone
to walk alongside with...

00:21:58.410 --> 00:22:00.870
The choices get narrowed down.

00:22:06.330 --> 00:22:10.120
I should choose whatever's best for me.

00:22:12.040 --> 00:22:16.450
It appears that Adachi has chosen the path
where she doesn't need anyone else...

00:22:22.290 --> 00:22:26.200
"Episode 11: 'The Moon and Determination,
Determination and Friends'"

00:22:26.200 --> 00:22:28.000
"Episode 11: 'The Moon and Determination,
Determination and Friends'"

00:22:26.200 --> 00:22:28.000
But I...

